# The considered-and-CLOSED records that must SURVIVE an edit: an option
# REJECTED, or DEFERRED under a stated trigger. Baseline for `mth check
# --records .spec-records SPEC.md`.
#
# `<id>` then whitespace then the marker, which runs to end of line and may
# contain spaces. `#` comments and blank lines are skipped.
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT A DERIVED RULE: every other structural rule asks "is
# this file well formed", which one text can answer. This one asks "is this
# record still here" -- a claim about EDITS OVER TIME, and no single text can
# say what used to be in it. So the checker owns the rule and this repo owns
# the list.
#
# The marker is a SUBSTRING of the record, not the whole thing: long enough
# to be specific, short enough that rewording the surrounding prose does not
# fire it. What must survive is the DECISION, not the sentence.
#
# WHY THESE FIVE ARE THE FRAGILE ONES: none of them describes anything itok
# builds, so to a compaction pass counting bytes they read as the most
# deletable text in the file -- pure "we weighed it and said no". Delete them
# and the spec stays internally consistent, every citation still resolves,
# and the gate stays green. Then someone re-proposes CIDR scanning and
# nothing says it was already answered. That is what V83 (best idea wins,
# make the COMPARISON auditable) rests on.
#
# DEFERRED is not a weaker REJECTED -- it is a different state, and the two
# are told apart by the trigger. V21 and V58 say `DEFERRED (⊥ rejected)` in
# their own text and each names the condition that reopens it. The deferred
# ones need this guard MORE: a rejection reads as a closed decision, while a
# deferral reads as an unbuilt feature, which is exactly what a byte-cutting
# pass drops thinking "not built = not needed". So the marker pinned for
# those two is the deferral itself.
#
# Adding a line here is how a new closed option becomes load-bearing.
# Removing one is a reviewed decision: it says the option is no longer worth
# recording, which is the trade this file exists to stop being made silently.

# DEFERRED -- trigger: a real fileset where greedy drops a better-fitting
# combination.
V21  DEFERRED

# REJECTED -- a subnet probe is a port scan; discovery is composed, not
# built in.
V24  rejected

# REJECTED -- `host[:port]` is already the convention; a flag cannot express
# per-host ports in a fleet list.
V25  rejected

# REJECTED -- a cloud count_tokens needs an API key and egresses file
# content. Escape hatch recorded, never a default.
V35  REJECTED

# DEFERRED -- trigger: a measured need for a signal only in-flight
# interception can give.
V58  DEFERRED
